// A task that waits in a receive with a limit can continue, because its limit
// can pass, so it prevents a deadlock (spec/04-semantics.md, Deadlock). The
// main task and `waiter` wait. `waiter` has no limit, and the main task has
// one: no program ends with DeadlockError while the limit can pass. The main
// task then gets TimeoutError and goes on.
// STATUS: ok
// TIMEOUT: 30
// CHECK: waiter waits
// CHECK: TimeoutError
// CHECK: main goes on
fun waiter() {
    print "waiter waits";
    task.receive();
}
task.spawn(waiter);
try {
    task.receive_within(0.2);
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}
print "main goes on";
